<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dewan Rakyat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Representatives of Malaysia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dewan Rakyat ('<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lok-sabha">House of the People</a>') is the lower house of the Parliament of Malaysia, with 222 members elected for up to five years from single-member constituencies. The prime minister must command its confidence, and it passes legislation and the budget, while the appointed upper house, the Dewan Negara, can only delay bills.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dewan-rakyat.jpg" alt="Dewan Rakyat" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.parlimen.gov.my/ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dewan_Rakyat.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
